  <s:String x:Key="Cli.Help" xml:space="preserve">aeris-cli: disk cleanup and analysis without a window. No network access, no telemetry.&#10;&#10;Usage:&#10;  aeris-cli scan &lt;folder&gt; [--top 200] [--min-size 100MB] [--type video|archive|installer|document|image] [--json] [--csv &lt;file&gt;]&#10;  aeris-cli clean [--categories id1,id2 | --profile &lt;name&gt;] [--older-than 2d] [--mode permanent|quarantine] [--dry-run] [--yes] [--json] [--quiet]&#10;  aeris-cli duplicates &lt;folder&gt;... [--min-size 1MB] [--json] [--delete-to-recycle --yes]&#10;  aeris-cli duplicates &lt;folder&gt;... --similar-images [--threshold 5] [--json]&#10;  aeris-cli empty-folders &lt;folder&gt;... [--keep-system-files] [--json] [--delete-to-recycle --yes]&#10;  aeris-cli history [--last 20] [--json]&#10;  aeris-cli restore &lt;operation-id&gt; [--yes]&#10;  aeris-cli categories [--json]&#10;&#10;clean shows the plan first and asks before deleting. Without a console it needs --yes. --dry-run only shows the plan.&#10;Personal files (duplicates, empty folders) are only reported unless you add --delete-to-recycle --yes; then they go to the Recycle Bin.&#10;&#10;Exit codes: 0 success, 1 done with skipped files or errors, 2 invalid arguments or refused, 3 cancelled.</s:String>
